 "subject": "Calculating coverage of genomic regions",
 "messages_listed": 5,
 "last_activity": "2017-10-26T03:11:32Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "Evgz26AuBAAJ",
   "from": "Linda Molla",
   "author": "ac5ddd29540c757f",
   "date": "2017-07-10T18:54:05Z",
   "subject": "Calculating coverage of genomic regions",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I am interested to know if methylkit can be used to find out the coverage of specific regions in the genome. For example of all the potential enhancers or promoters rich in CpGs in a reference genome (example annotated promoters or enhancers in mouse genome)  how many of them are actually well covered through the ERRBS sequencing<div>If this is not possible through methylkit any recommendations on how to do this using the ERRBS data?</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Thank you,</div><div>Linda</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "UmoVzNeFBAAJ",
   "from": "Altuna Akalin",
   "author": "ab8277113f65c05e",
   "date": "2017-07-11T12:30:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: [methylkit_discussion] Calculating coverage of genomic regions",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">you can use regionCounts() if you have the locations of the specific regions you are interested in. you can also coerce methylKit objects to GRanges objects and use findOverlaps or subsetByoverlaps from GenomicRanges package.</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Jul 10, 2017 at 8:54 PM, Linda Molla <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">molla...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I am interested to know if methylkit can be used to find out the coverage of specific regions in the genome. For example of all the potential enhancers or promoters rich in CpGs in a reference genome (example annotated promoters or enhancers in mouse genome)  how many of them are actually well covered through the ERRBS sequencing<div>If this is not possible through methylkit any recommendations on how to do this using the ERRBS data?</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Thank you,</div><div>Linda</div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><br></div></font></span></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
