   "id": "sSL8lyL6AAAJ",
   "from": "Altuna Akalin",
   "author": "ab8277113f65c05e",
   "date": "2017-10-14T06:45:21Z",
   "subject": "Re: [methylkit_discussion] Calculating coverage of genomic regions",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">if you want to calculate what percentage of genomic features is covered by CpGs with methylation calls, you can just use methylRaw object, convert it to GRanges with as(...,&quot;GRanges&quot;). Then you can use GenomicRanges::findOverlaps or something similar to figure out what percentage of features are covered.<div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Altuna</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sat, Oct 14, 2017 at 1:37 AM, Linda Molla <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">molla...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
